            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "Before the new one: say the Russian for a chance, then the Russian for a risk."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "index": 1,
          "type": "input",
          "title": "You'll want to know: рисковать",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "рисковать (riskovát) — \"to take a risk, to risk\"."
            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "Я не хочу рисковать своими деньгами. Ya ne khochú riskovát svoími dengámi. I do not want to risk my money."
            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "Imperfective; the present is рискую, рискуешь; perfective рискнуть. Рисковать + instrumental — to risk something."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "index": 2,
          "type": "etymology",
          "title": "The word, taken apart",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "рисковать (riskovát) \"to risk\" (EtymDB) is built on риск, which is usually traced, through French risque, to Italian risco."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "index": 3,
          "type": "notice",
          "title": "What you've built",
          "segments": [
