          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "опасаться (opasátsya) — \"to fear, to be wary of\"."
            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "Врачи опасаются новой эпидемии. Vrachí opasáyutsya nóvoy epidémii. Doctors fear a new epidemic."
            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "Imperfective only. It takes the genitive: опасаться (opasátsya) дождя. More formal than бояться."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "index": 2,
          "type": "etymology",
          "title": "The word, taken apart",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "опасаться (opasátsya) is usually traced to о- and пасти \"to guard, to watch over\", inherited from Proto-Slavic pasti (EtymDB): to be wary is to keep watch. Опасный \"dangerous\" is built on it."
            }
          ]
        },
