              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "угрожать (ugrozhát) — \"to threaten\"."
            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "Сильный ветер угрожает старым деревьям. Sílnyy véter ugrozháyet stárym derévyam. The strong wind threatens the old trees."
            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "Imperfective. Угрожать кому чем: the person threatened goes in the dative. The noun is угроза, a threat."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "index": 2,
          "type": "etymology",
          "title": "The word, taken apart",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "угрожать (ugrozhát) is built from у- and гроза \"a thunderstorm\", which in older Russian also meant terror and threat; з softens to ж in the verb."
            }
          ]
        },
